# Requests to try against the running server, one block at a time.
# [BEGINNER] Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
# and click "Send Request" above a block. `npm run dev` must be running.
# (JetBrains IDEs run .http files natively.) Blocks are separated by lines starting with ###.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Hello → 200 and a line of text
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2. List users → 200 and [] (an empty JSON array) after a restart
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### 3. Create a user → 201
# [BEGINNER] A POST has a body. The empty line after the headers is required: it separates the
# headers from the body. Content-Type tells the server that the body is JSON.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ann", "email": "ann@test.io" }

### 4. Create a user with NO data → 201 as well (nothing checks the data yet)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{}
